  "prompt_prefix": "",
  "instruction": "In the two years 2022/2023, which Canadian province had the largest total capital expenditure in hydroelectric power generation over that time?",
  "answer": "Based on the Statistics Canada data (Table 34-10-0063-01), here are the hydro-electric power plant capital expenditures by province for 2022 (in millions of dollars):\n\n**2022:**\n- British Columbia: **$2,742.0M**\n- Quebec: $1,071.4M\n- Ontario: $792.5M\n- Manitoba: $302.2M\n- Nova Scotia: $99.7M\n- Newfoundland and Labrador: $42.2M\n- Saskatchewan: $7.2M\n- New Brunswick, Alberta, Yukon, NWT: suppressed (confidential)\n\n**2023:**\n- Ontario: $885.6M\n- All other provinces/territories: suppressed (confidential)\n\nCanada total: $5,190.3M (2022) and $5,017.0M (2023).\n\n**Answer: British Columbia** had the largest hydro-electric capital expenditure in 2022 at **$2.74 billion** — over half of Canada's total. While most 2023 provincial figures are suppressed, BC's Site C project (a $16B project under active construction through 2023) and the StatCan article identifying BC as a major driver of hydro investment strongly indicate BC remained the largest in 2023 as well.",
